# The names Flint's own tests gave their scratch folders in the system temp
# folder, before every test run had one folder of its own to clean up
# (test-support/temp-root.ts for vitest, apps/studio/test/temp_root.zsh for the
# studio's script tests). One prefix on a line.
#
# apps/studio/free_space.sh reads this list to find what those tests left
# behind. A folder is one of them only when its whole name is a prefix here
# followed by exactly the six characters mkdtemp or mktemp adds, at least one
# of them a digit or a capital; it sits directly in the temp folder; it is this
# user's; nothing in it has changed for a day; and it holds no socket.
#
# Every prefix here starts with flint-. The tests also used short, plain names
# (ws-, tok-, export-, install- and some forty more): another program may use
# those too, so they are not listed, and a folder with such a name is never
# removed. What they left is the system's to clear.
#
# A new test needs no line here: what it makes now lands inside its run's own
# folder, which is removed when the run ends. The two lines that matter from
# here on are the run folders themselves (a run that was killed leaves its one):
flint-t-
flint-t.
